[2026-10-20T07:59:06.368Z] [safeoutputs] recv: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"add_comment","arguments":{"body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** not attempted: this is a style/feature request, and the issue gives no unexpected Black output to reproduce (the \"current style\" example is standard Black output).\n**Assessment:** The behaviour described is deliberate. Black wraps lines uniformly and puts one element per line (with trailing commas) when a bracketed expression doesn't fit, which keeps diffs small. The style docs also say configuration options are deliberately limited and rarely added, so a new `no-short-lines` / `min-line-length` option runs against that design. See \"How Black wraps lines\" in the current style docs: https://black.vercel.app/ (docs at black.readthedocs.io, `the_black_code_style/current_style`).\n**Next step:** Maintainers can weigh whether the proposal justifies a new option. Meanwhile, if you want to control the layout in specific places, removing the magic trailing comma lets Black collapse a collection that fits on one line.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: `R: not a bug` (or a decision on whether to accept a new option)</sub>"}}}
